A||N||1||Vlad||Rear tranny mount||||5||
Z||000000||Vlad||01-23-2001||01:02 AM||||Hello<P>After hearing a loud bumping noise when shifting into Drive and checking tranny mounts, I know that rear mount is dead. The rubber part is just sliced into two separate pieces. Going to replace it, but........<BR>Even though I read that this is not a big job, it seems almost impossible to me. <BR>Those 3 bracket-tranny bolts are reachable and two big mount-frame nuts are free of rust. <BR>But how the heck I get to the big nut that secures rubber to frame. I didn't find the way to access it...(<P>Please, if anybody has anything to say, do not hesitate...<P>85 GT Auto||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||01-23-2001||08:58 AM||||i replaced the mounts on my '86 GT, 5 speed.  not knowing which car you have, i am going to assume that they are the same.<P>there are three bolts that hold the rubber mount to the cradle, and one that holds the mount to the tranny bracket.<P>here is what i did:<P>1) jack up the rear of the car, placing jack stands under the left and right sides of the cradle.  make sure to remove the rear tires, as this will remove any unnecessary weight from the half shafts.<P>2) remove the nut on the bolt holding the mount to the bracket, you need to use a box end wrench (i forget the size, but think it is a 15 mm).  you can't get a full turn but you can losen and remove the nut.<P>3) the three nuts mounting to the cradle are accesible and can be removed with a 13 mm socket.<P>4) at this point, you will need to jack up the tranny.  place a small piece of 2x4 between the jack and the housing, and jack the tranny up enough to allowthe bracket to seperate from the mount.<P>5) at this point you can swap in the new mount and reverse the proceedure to complete the job.<P>If for any reason the the bracket doesn't easily clear the mount, you may need to loosen the bolts that hold the bracket to the tranny, this will give you some extra play.<P>Also, be aware that you do not have to buy tranny mounts from the Fiero Store!  Check with your local auto parts store, you will be surprised.  I bought the rear mount from Auto Zone for $9!  Thats a lot less than the Fiero Store wants for the same thing.<P>Best of luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
